<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>South Fork Shelter</name><desc>or-central-meissner-1984:51: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.031730" lon="-121.514972"><ele>1445.1</ele><name>Skyliner Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:skyliner-snow-play (OSM node 2898613043 Skyliners Trailhead parking); confidence: high; pdf_page: 104; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: Ski to Tumalo Falls, parking at Skyliner snow-play area.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.031112" lon="-121.519601"><ele>1448.6</ele><name>Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Skyliners Road way 5371804, start of Bear Wallow Road way 5371530 (as in or-vielbig-2e_276-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 102; quote: Follow the directions for skiing to Tumalo Falls.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.032192" lon="-121.521312"><ele>1442.9</ele><name>North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate)</name><desc>source: OSM: Bear Wallow Road bridge way 189478515; Tumalo Falls Road NF 4603 (way 279479047) leaves here (as in or-vielbig-2e_276-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 105; quote: sketch map: road 4603 along the north side of Tumalo Creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.031904" lon="-121.566371"><ele>1517.8</ele><name>Tumalo Falls picnic area (road end, bridge)</name><desc>source: OSM: west end of Tumalo Falls Road (way 5370497) across the road bridge way 279479046 (as in or-vielbig-2e_276-1); confidence: high; pdf_page: 104; quote: After crossing the bridge over Tumalo Creek, at the picnic area, the ski trail goes sharply to the left just across the bridge.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.027901" lon="-121.560435"><ele>1504.5</ele><name>Tumalo Creek Trail #25.1 / South Fork Trail #25 junction</name><desc>source: OSM: end of Tumalo Creek Trail #25.1 way 279480189, start of South Fork Trail #25 way 840623247; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 104; quote: A short distance down-stream is a small bridge which crosses Bridge Creek. Cross the bridge and go left. The ski trail crosses the burned area to the trees on the south.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.023889" lon="-121.566963"><ele>1551.0</ele><name>South Fork Shelter (site, placed)</name><desc>source: Not mapped (shelter gone). Placed on South Fork Trail #25 (OSM vertex), 0.5 mi above the Tumalo Creek Trail junction: the text's 'about 1/2 mile' beside the creek, and sketch map 105 (scaled by road 4603) puts it about 0.55 mi south of the falls bridge on the South Fork; DEM 5,089 ft vs the book's 5,000; confidence: low; pdf_page: 105; book_elev_ft: 5000; quote: Just back into the trees is the south fork of Tumalo Creek. If snow conditions are good you can ski on the side of the creek to the shelter (about 1/2 mile).</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>South Fork Shelter</name><desc>1. Skyliner Sno-Park -&gt; Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction: osm (high), 0.24 mi | 2. Skyliners Road / Bear Wallow Road junction -&gt; North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate): osm (high), 0.11 mi | 3. North end of the Tumalo Creek bridge (road 4603 gate) -&gt; Tumalo Falls picnic area (road end, bridge): osm (high), 2.44 mi | 4. Tumalo Falls picnic area (road end, bridge) -&gt; Tumalo Creek Trail #25.1 / South Fork Trail #25 junction: osm (medium), 0.43 mi | 5. Tumalo Creek Trail #25.1 / South Fork Trail #25 junction -&gt; South Fork Shelter (site, placed): osm (medium), 0.49 mi</desc>
